/*
The objective of this script is to set up a clean, structured foundation for a Data Warehouse using the industry-standard Medallion Architecture (Multi-Hop Architecture).

What the Script Does
Environment Reset (Idempotency):

Checks if an older version of the DataWarehouse database exists.

Kills any active user connections immediately and deletes it to ensure you start from a 100% clean state without leftover test tables or broken dependencies.

Database Provisioning:

Creates a brand-new, empty DataWarehouse database.

Data Layering (Logical Separation):

Defines three distinct schemas (bronze, silver, gold) to organize data by its level of quality and readiness.
*/


USE master;
GO

IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.databases WHERE name = 'DataWarehouse')
BEGIN
	ALTER DATABASE DataWarehouse SET SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE;
	DROP DATABASE DataWarehouse;
	END;
	GO

USE DataWarehouse;
GO

CREATE SCHEMA bronze;
GO

CREATE SCHEMA silver;
GO

CREATE SCHEMA gold;
GO
